org/obo/mondo/sparql/omimps-should-be-inherited-violation.sparql\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:657:| IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/disease_series_by_gene.yaml |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:658:| Name | disease_series_by_gene |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:670:| IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/disease_series_by_gene.yaml |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:671:| Name | disease_series_by_gene_and_inheritance |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:675:| Examples | [mondo](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/blob/master/src/patterns/data/matches/disease_series_by_gene_and_inheritance.tsv) |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:686:See full table [here](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/blob/master/src/patterns/data/matches/disease_series_by_gene_and_inheritance.tsv)\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:949:*This pattern should be used for children of MONDO_0020573'inherited disease susceptibility', including OMIM phenotypic series (OMIMPS) for which the subclasses are susceptibilities. Note, this pattern should not have an asserted causative gene as logical axiom (and no single causative gene in text definition), in those cases, the susceptibility_by_gene pattern should be used instead. The children should have asserted causative genes in the text definitions and in the logical axioms. This pattern is a superclass of the susceptibility_by_gene pattern.\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:1485:| IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene.yaml |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:1486:| Name | nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:1984:| IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/susceptibility_by_gene.yaml |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:1985:| Name | susceptibility_by_gene |\nsrc/patterns/dosdp-patterns/README.md:1989:| Examples | [mondo](https://github.com/monarch-initia